  "prompt": "How does each lead source convert through the 2025 sales funnel? Take the leads created in 2025 (created_at, Brussels local time); a contact counts under every source it had a 2025 lead from. A contact is one email address, compared exactly as stored. A contact counts as with_opportunity when one of its leads from that source has an opportunity, and as won when one of those opportunities is won. The steps need no date order: an opportunity counts whenever it was created, and a won one whenever it closed, even in a later year. Return seven columns, in this order: source, contacts, with_opportunity, won (each a number of contacts), opportunity_rate (with_opportunity over contacts), win_rate (won over with_opportunity) and overall_rate (won over contacts), each rate a fraction between 0 and 1; win_rate is missing for a source with no contact with an opportunity. Return one row for each source. Any row order is fine.",
